# Bench: one K-type TC on an Adafruit AD8495 breakout, OUT -> AIN10 (J5 pad 6), Vin -> J2 pad 1, GND -> J5 GND.
# 2026-10-20 boil read 95.3 C vs 99.8, BUT the TC plug reached the amp through breadboard + copper jumpers,
# which moves the cold junction to the plug (steam-warmed) -> that +4.48 was mostly wiring error. Reset to 0.
# Re-calibrate only with K wire / K socket all the way into the amp's screw terminals.
# Probe: K-TEST (bench test probe, no serial, not a flight sensor). Any bias here is NOT a flight calibration.
configs { channel: 10  assignment: TC002  tc_type: K_TYPE  tc_bias_deg_c: 0 }
